  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian Agency for Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics (BMKG) has issued updated forecasts indicating that light rain will likely cover large portions of the country, including the Greater Jakarta area, known as Jabodetabek, on Wednesday, November 25, 2026. This comes as the agency maintains cautionary alerts regarding the potential for extreme weather, including heavy precipitation, which is projected to persist in various Indonesian regions through the end of November 2026. While widespread light rain is expected, environmental authorities are also managing local incidents, such as reported ash fall in Klapanunggal, Bogor, which has been submitted for laboratory analysis. The current meteorological outlook follows earlier significant weather events in November that resulted in casualties and localized infrastructure disruption, prompting authorities to continue monitoring atmospheric conditions closely across the archipelago.",
